## Australian Office of Financial Management source material

The packaged Excel snapshots in `inst/extdata/` and the related entries in the
package's AOFM source catalogue are Commonwealth material published by the
Australian Office of Financial Management (AOFM) Data Hub. The AOFM copyright
notice states that AOFM material is provided under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International licence, with exclusions for the Commonwealth
Coat of Arms, the AOFM logo, trademarks, and content supplied by third parties:
<https://www.aofm.gov.au/copyright>.

Attribute these snapshots and source records to **Australian Office of
Financial Management** and link to the applicable source. The package is an
independent project; attribution must not imply Commonwealth or AOFM
endorsement, sponsorship, or affiliation. Third-party rights may remain with
their owners and may require separate permission. Check the current AOFM
notice and source terms before redistributing or relying on a snapshot.

The five packaged snapshots and their original acquisition URLs are listed
below. These retired `/media/` routes are retained only as historical
provenance for the exact bundled bytes; they are not the package's current
runtime catalogue routes. Current direct Data Hub routes and byte comparisons
are recorded in `inst/extdata/README.md`.

* `tb_issuance.xlsx` — <https://www.aofm.gov.au/media/591>
* `tb_position_dealt.xlsx` — <https://www.aofm.gov.au/media/578>
* `tb_syndication.xlsx` — <https://www.aofm.gov.au/media/632>
* `tib_issuance.xlsx` — <https://www.aofm.gov.au/media/429>
* `tib_syndication.xlsx` — <https://www.aofm.gov.au/media/631>

These AOFM workbooks and source records are not relicensed under the
readAOFM MIT licence.

The rendered Treasury Bond chart in `man/figures/` is derived from
`tb_issuance.xlsx`. Its source caption attributes the Australian Office of
Financial Management and the AOFM Data Hub. The underlying observations remain
Commonwealth material under the terms and exclusions described above; the
generated visualisation does not imply AOFM endorsement.

